.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt STDCKDINT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ckd_add ,
.Nm ckd_sub ,
.Nm ckd_mul
.Nd checked integer arithmetic
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdckdint.h
.Ft bool
.Fn ckd_add "result" "a" "b"
.Ft bool
.Fn ckd_sub "result" "a" "b"
.Ft bool
.Fn ckd_mul "result" "a" "b"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.In stdckdint.h
header provides macros for arithmetic with overflow detection.
Each macro evaluates its two operands at their mathematical value,
converts the exact result to the type of the object designated by
.Fa result ,
stores that converted value, and yields
.Dv true
exactly when the conversion is not value preserving.
Every argument is evaluated exactly once and no operation has undefined
behaviour, even when the mathematical result is not representable in any
integer type.
.Pp
The macros accept any integer types; the operands need not have the same
type, and
.Fa result
may be narrower, wider or of a different signedness than the operands.
When the result type is unsigned and the exact value is out of range, the
stored value wraps modulo the width of the type and the macro yields
.Dv true .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ckd_add ,
.Fn ckd_sub
and
.Fn ckd_mul
return a value of type
.Vt bool :
.Dv true
if the result could not be represented in the destination type,
.Dv false
otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The following stores the sum of two
.Vt int
values only when it fits:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int sum;

if (!ckd_add(&sum, a, b))
	use(sum);
else
	overflow();
.Ed
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.In stdckdint.h
header conforms to ISO/IEC 9899:2024 (C23).
.Sh HISTORY
The
.In stdckdint.h
header appeared in
.Ox 8.0 .
